WEBVTT

00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:21.060
I've located our target, Birdy.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:23.060
This time I'm not letting them get away!

00:00:26.070 --> 00:00:28.470
They're fast! This is hopeless, Boss!

00:00:28.470 --> 00:00:30.570
This ship can't outrun
a Federation investigator!

00:00:30.570 --> 00:00:32.740
It's too late to whine about that now!

00:00:32.740 --> 00:00:34.510
Now listen up; I'm only gonna say this once.

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:36.210
Shake 'em off!

00:00:36.210 --> 00:00:41.580
Geega, I'm hungry. Can I eat this guy?

00:00:41.580 --> 00:00:47.920
Hold on, Bacillus. I'll let you
eat this idiot if he stops the ship.

00:00:47.920 --> 00:00:49.920
Here it comes, Birdy.

00:00:57.030 --> 00:00:58.860
Now I'm pissed!

00:01:04.710 --> 00:01:06.010
I'm going out there, Tuto.

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:07.410
Roger.

00:01:19.190 --> 00:01:21.590
The investigator's boarded the ship!

00:01:35.910 --> 00:01:37.240
She's here!

00:01:37.240 --> 00:01:39.780
You caused me trouble...

00:01:39.780 --> 00:01:42.210
I assume you're prepared for the consequences?

00:01:45.150 --> 00:01:47.880
You ignored a Federation
investigator's order to halt the ship!

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:50.150
And then you put up armed resistance!

00:01:50.150 --> 00:01:53.290
You'd better be ready for
fifty years' penal servitude!

00:01:53.290 --> 00:01:56.460
Well? Where's Geega?

00:01:56.460 --> 00:02:01.330
Hey! Where are Geega and Bacillus?! Answer me!

00:02:01.330 --> 00:02:03.170
I... I!

00:02:03.170 --> 00:02:05.600
Birdy, it's an escape pod!

00:02:09.310 --> 00:02:11.640
Hey! Do something, Tuto!

00:02:11.640 --> 00:02:12.630
It's no good.

00:02:14.510 --> 00:02:15.580
They jumped.

00:02:15.580 --> 00:02:16.980
That Geega...

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:26.290
<i>Will the sky one day grow tired of</i>
<i>looking down and lose its blue color?</i>

00:02:26.290 --> 00:02:35.290
<i>There's just one blue sky over this</i>
<i>world rife with countless emotions</i>

00:02:39.200 --> 00:02:42.310
<i>The sound of the battle raging somewhere</i>

00:02:42.310 --> 00:02:45.270
<i>And the laughter right nearby</i>

00:02:45.270 --> 00:02:48.210
<i>You can never hear it all</i>

00:02:48.210 --> 00:02:50.810
<i>Because you have only one story</i>

00:02:50.810 --> 00:02:56.720
<i>Only this sky sees all at</i>
<i>once the sorrow and smiles</i>

00:02:56.720 --> 00:03:02.690
<i>That simultaneously fall in different</i>
<i>places around this wide world</i>

00:03:02.690 --> 00:03:09.170
<i>Will the sky one day grow tired of</i>
<i>looking down and lose its blue color?</i>

00:03:09.170 --> 00:03:15.040
<i>How can it stay unchanging after</i>
<i>watching innumerable dramas?</i>

00:03:15.040 --> 00:03:21.310
<i>Even now everyone heads to his</i>
<i>own story without knowing a thing</i>

00:03:21.310 --> 00:03:29.510
<i>There's just one blue sky over this</i>
<i>world rife with countless emotions</i>

00:03:30.250 --> 00:03:40.690
<i>Wordlessly marking out</i>
<i>time longer than anyone's...</i>

00:04:05.560 --> 00:04:07.550
"Photography Schedule"
"Shion Arita"

00:04:08.690 --> 00:04:11.690
Okay, thanks for everything, Yamamoto baby!

00:04:11.690 --> 00:04:14.030
She was great again today, Satoru baby.

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:17.070
We've got nothing to worry
about with <i>you</i> behind the camera!

00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:19.700
Would Shion like to join us for lunch?

00:04:19.700 --> 00:04:24.770
Baby, I'll go with you if we can
leave Shion behind and make it a date!

00:04:24.770 --> 00:04:26.040
I'll pass.

00:04:26.040 --> 00:04:27.740
Thank you for waiting, Sirs.

00:04:27.740 --> 00:04:29.250
Good work today, girl.

00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:31.450
Yes, Sir!

00:04:31.450 --> 00:04:33.320
Good afternoon, yessiree.

00:04:33.320 --> 00:04:35.320
Good work today, Shion baby.

00:04:35.320 --> 00:04:38.250
Okay, toodles!

00:04:38.250 --> 00:04:39.890
Shion was sure a big hit when she went on TV,

00:04:39.890 --> 00:04:42.490
even if it was just a late show, huh?

00:04:42.490 --> 00:04:46.300
Yeah, that was great.
The airheaded alien character!

00:04:46.300 --> 00:04:49.000
I hear she made quite a splash on the internet.

00:04:49.000 --> 00:04:53.000
But they say she's turned
down all TV work since then.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:54.770
What a waste!

00:04:54.770 --> 00:04:57.600
They're biding their time to sell
her when she'll rake in the most.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:03.280
I'm starving...

00:05:05.820 --> 00:05:08.450
Oh, Shion Arita is so <i>cute!</i>

00:05:08.450 --> 00:05:10.920
- Shion...
- I'll have to buy two of these, so I can save one!

00:05:10.920 --> 00:05:13.620
Oh? I'm gonna buy three. She's drool-worthy!

00:05:13.620 --> 00:05:15.020
Hey, Senkawa!

00:05:15.020 --> 00:05:17.960
What do you say to
Shiorin's amazing gorgeousness?!

00:05:17.960 --> 00:05:18.960
Whatever.

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:20.700
Ugh, this is the problem
with gloomy types like you!

00:05:20.700 --> 00:05:25.770
Look! This is Shiorin, the most
popular star in Akihabara right now!

00:05:25.770 --> 00:05:27.200
Well, Senkawa?!

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:28.600
She's not my type.

00:05:28.600 --> 00:05:30.540
Are you blind, man?!

00:05:30.540 --> 00:05:32.340
She's older than my big sister...

00:05:32.340 --> 00:05:35.650
You moron! Listen, age is irrelevant with pop stars!

00:05:35.650 --> 00:05:38.380
Man, I can't believe you're looking at this stuff.

00:05:38.380 --> 00:05:39.180
Hayamiya...

00:05:39.180 --> 00:05:42.650
Jeez, the second you got to high
school you started getting into girls.

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:45.790
Hey, this is Shion, the one
who plays the stupid alien!

00:05:45.790 --> 00:05:49.530
What?! That's just rude,
calling her "stupid," Hayamiya!

00:05:49.530 --> 00:05:50.490
Call her an "airhead"!

00:05:50.490 --> 00:05:51.890
This stuff, please.

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:55.870
Hurry up!

00:05:55.870 --> 00:05:58.070
I'm starving!

00:05:58.070 --> 00:06:00.740
Yeah, yeah. Good work today.

00:06:00.740 --> 00:06:03.240
Is there really any point in doing this crap?

00:06:03.240 --> 00:06:07.380
That's no way to talk!
We know Geega is on this planet.

00:06:07.380 --> 00:06:10.150
It's been six months.

00:06:10.150 --> 00:06:12.420
In Oriotera time...

00:06:12.420 --> 00:06:16.750
I mean, in Earth time,
it's been five months and 25 days.

00:06:16.750 --> 00:06:23.190
Our investigation is getting
steadily closer to its goal, Birdy.

00:06:23.190 --> 00:06:26.060
How long do I have to do this stuff?!

00:06:26.060 --> 00:06:29.330
Undercover investigations take time.

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:33.700
Geega has hidden himself in the
entertainment world of this planet.

00:06:33.700 --> 00:06:38.610
That's info from Irma, though, right?
Is she really an Altan?

00:06:38.610 --> 00:06:41.580
DNA data confirms it.

00:06:41.580 --> 00:06:46.220
This planet called "Earth" has a
civilization rating of six, which is low,

00:06:46.220 --> 00:06:49.290
but there seem to be a lot of illegal
immigrants from the Federation.

00:06:49.290 --> 00:06:52.420
They're living here disguised as Earthlings.

00:06:52.420 --> 00:06:55.690
On this hick planet out in the boonies, huh?

00:06:55.690 --> 00:06:58.890
I think this place is actually pretty interesting.

00:06:58.890 --> 00:07:00.930
Well, I don't like it.

00:07:00.930 --> 00:07:04.920
If I stay here I just know I'll
end up an ugly hag like Irma.

00:07:07.440 --> 00:07:11.570
What a thing to say, Birdy.

00:07:11.570 --> 00:07:17.780
And here I'm helping you out with
your investigation as a fellow Altan!

00:07:17.780 --> 00:07:23.550
Here on Earth I'm quite famous
among ex-Federationers, you know.

00:07:23.550 --> 00:07:27.960
A youngster like you has no
business calling me a "hag."

00:07:27.960 --> 00:07:29.490
I'm sorry.

00:07:29.490 --> 00:07:33.630
Okay, Tuto, hand over today's earnings.

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:36.230
What, this is all?

00:07:36.230 --> 00:07:38.400
If you don't earn good money as Shion Arita,

00:07:38.400 --> 00:07:43.270
you may be stuck living here forever.

00:07:43.270 --> 00:07:47.910
I'll work! I'll gladly be Shion Arita!

00:07:47.910 --> 00:07:53.080
Good girl, Birdy.
Maybe I'll give you a little reward.

00:07:53.080 --> 00:07:53.350
"Empire Television"
"Kunio Giga"

00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:54.650
Here.

00:07:54.650 --> 00:07:59.120
Sounds like that Giga guy isn't from this planet.

00:07:59.120 --> 00:08:01.960
Empire Television...

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:04.790
It's been almost a year, hasn't it, Mr. Giga?

00:08:07.030 --> 00:08:11.330
I'm a patient man, but I
need to see some results soon.

00:08:11.330 --> 00:08:13.470
Otherwise I can't justify myself to my investors.

00:08:13.470 --> 00:08:16.440
But the scientists here are so low-level.

00:08:16.440 --> 00:08:20.340
It's going to take more time to
find out how to grow the Ryunka.

00:08:20.340 --> 00:08:23.510
And it's gotten harder to secure food for it!

00:08:23.510 --> 00:08:26.320
What, an alien like you is afraid of the police?

00:08:26.320 --> 00:08:29.720
There might be a Federation
investigator on this planet!

00:08:32.560 --> 00:08:37.560
There are lots of aliens here, huh?
Sounds entertaining.

00:08:37.560 --> 00:08:41.500
It sounds entertaining, so let's
raise the Ryunka as fast as we can.

00:08:41.500 --> 00:08:44.130
I'm sure Gomez will be surprised, too.

00:08:46.740 --> 00:08:50.360
I look forward to it. It promises to
be more amusing than marionettes.

00:08:55.580 --> 00:08:59.920
Well, Tuto? What's the word on this "Giga" guy?

00:08:59.920 --> 00:09:03.920
He just came out. A car is here to pick him up.

00:09:03.920 --> 00:09:07.520
It looks like he was being wooed by
an entertainment production company.

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:11.560
Two men have come to get him.

00:09:11.560 --> 00:09:12.550
Oh, I see.

00:09:17.070 --> 00:09:20.700
There they go. Don't lose sight of them.

00:09:20.700 --> 00:09:21.500
Follow that car!

00:09:21.500 --> 00:09:23.440
"String of New Celebs Mysteriously Disappears!!"

00:09:23.440 --> 00:09:26.270
This time they're <i>not</i> getting away!

00:09:55.910 --> 00:09:58.070
Your car is really the best, Boss!

00:09:58.070 --> 00:10:02.210
Ya got that right! It's totally bulletproof, too!

00:10:02.210 --> 00:10:04.980
What is it, Boss? Whoa!

00:10:04.980 --> 00:10:05.970
Why me?

00:10:08.450 --> 00:10:11.990
Now this is some nice crumbling!

00:10:11.990 --> 00:10:15.560
Masakubo and Hazawa are sure late...

00:10:15.560 --> 00:10:18.060
Huh?

00:10:18.060 --> 00:10:19.050
Oh, a text.

00:10:21.000 --> 00:10:22.000
"Inbox" "Masakubo" "Sorry!"
"There's an event in Akihabara tomorrow,

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:22.500
so Hazawa and I are going to wait
in line all night!! Go ahead and explore
the ruined hotel by yourself."

00:10:22.500 --> 00:10:24.470
What the heck?

00:10:24.470 --> 00:10:25.970
Well, whatever.

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:27.600
Hey there, runaway boy!

00:10:27.600 --> 00:10:28.740
Hayamiya!

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:31.610
What are you doing in a place like this, Senkawa?

00:10:31.610 --> 00:10:32.940
What does it matter?

00:10:32.940 --> 00:10:34.610
Don't avoid my eyes!

00:10:34.610 --> 00:10:38.010
Exploring an abandoned building? How lame.

00:10:38.010 --> 00:10:39.010
Go home, then.

00:10:39.010 --> 00:10:40.120
Are you going in through here?

00:10:40.120 --> 00:10:40.850
Yeah.

00:10:40.850 --> 00:10:42.520
Sheesh, you're such a kid.

00:10:42.520 --> 00:10:45.420
Just go home, already.

00:10:45.420 --> 00:10:47.410
Hey, wait a second!

00:10:49.160 --> 00:10:51.090
Abandoned buildings in the city

00:10:51.090 --> 00:10:55.600
might be a good scoop for the Journalism Club.

00:10:55.600 --> 00:10:57.430
What are you doing?

00:10:59.970 --> 00:11:01.700
My ass is stuck.

00:11:01.700 --> 00:11:03.670
Don't say "ass."

00:11:03.670 --> 00:11:06.480
Come on, Senkawa, pull me through!

00:11:06.480 --> 00:11:07.610
Go home.

00:11:07.610 --> 00:11:08.600
Senkawa!

00:11:14.320 --> 00:11:19.050
Ugh! It's filthy and it smells like mold!

00:11:19.050 --> 00:11:20.990
It's great.

00:11:20.990 --> 00:11:23.530
What's so fun about a place like this?

00:11:23.530 --> 00:11:26.230
How should I put this?

00:11:26.230 --> 00:11:29.570
Abandoned buildings are like dead things.

00:11:29.570 --> 00:11:30.800
Dead?

00:11:30.800 --> 00:11:31.870
Right.

00:11:31.870 --> 00:11:36.710
As soon as things that were in use
leave human hands, they start to die.

00:11:36.710 --> 00:11:37.640
You get me?

00:11:37.640 --> 00:11:39.070
No, I don't.

00:11:39.070 --> 00:11:41.070
What are you doing there?!

00:11:44.180 --> 00:11:48.520
This is no place for kids to play!
The sign said "Keep Out," didn't it?!

00:11:48.520 --> 00:11:49.420
We're sorry.

00:11:49.420 --> 00:11:51.150
You don't have to shout at us!

00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:54.190
This building belongs to Empire TV!

00:11:54.190 --> 00:11:57.830
If you don't scram right now,
I'll turn you over to the police!

00:11:57.830 --> 00:12:01.060
Where do you get off?!
If this place is so precious...

00:12:01.060 --> 00:12:03.100
Forget it, Hayamiya.

00:12:03.100 --> 00:12:08.090
We're very sorry. We won't
come back again. Please excuse us.

00:12:10.410 --> 00:12:14.710
Dammit, kids are so much trouble...

00:12:14.710 --> 00:12:16.950
Where does he get off talking so big?!

00:12:16.950 --> 00:12:20.120
We're the ones in the wrong, so we can't complain.

00:12:20.120 --> 00:12:22.520
Honestly, why are you always like that?

00:12:22.520 --> 00:12:24.420
You wanted to explore, right?!

00:12:24.420 --> 00:12:27.890
Abandoned buildings are "abandoned"
because nobody's using them!

00:12:27.890 --> 00:12:29.690
This place doesn't qualify anymore.

00:12:29.690 --> 00:12:31.090
What?

00:12:41.040 --> 00:12:44.470
I guess they wouldn't be here...

00:12:44.470 --> 00:12:46.310
Mr. Giga?

00:12:46.310 --> 00:12:49.310
We meet at last! I've been looking for you.

00:12:49.310 --> 00:12:53.580
I'd just love for you to use my girl on Empire TV!

00:12:53.580 --> 00:12:56.890
Come here, Shion.

00:12:56.890 --> 00:12:59.320
I'm Shion Arita, yessiree!

00:12:59.320 --> 00:13:00.990
Who are you people?

00:13:00.990 --> 00:13:04.660
Aw, you don't remember me, Sir?!

00:13:04.660 --> 00:13:08.660
I'm so sad, yessiree!

00:13:08.660 --> 00:13:11.570
Hey, Geega.

00:13:11.570 --> 00:13:13.760
This time I'm not letting you go!

00:13:21.910 --> 00:13:24.650
There's still time.

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:29.150
If you come along quietly, you'll
only get, what, maybe 160 years?

00:13:29.150 --> 00:13:31.750
Birdy the Berserker Killer...

00:13:31.750 --> 00:13:36.490
But if you plan on defying me,
you'd better say your prayers.

00:13:36.490 --> 00:13:39.960
I had to come out to this
hick planet because of you,

00:13:39.960 --> 00:13:42.800
and I've built up lots of stress!

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:46.500
Who cares? I like this place!

00:13:46.500 --> 00:13:48.940
Get lost, you Federation dog.

00:14:08.360 --> 00:14:11.190
That'll add another five years to your sentence.

00:14:16.670 --> 00:14:20.840
He's using pretty cheap marionettes.

00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:24.970
Maybe I'm a little out of shape after all...

00:14:24.970 --> 00:14:30.050
Damn. Well, up against an lxioran Altan...

00:14:30.050 --> 00:14:31.030
Gross.

00:14:42.690 --> 00:14:46.900
Birdy, he's undergone biological alterations.

00:14:46.900 --> 00:14:50.030
That's not so bad, is it?
Makes him a worthier opponent.

00:14:50.030 --> 00:14:53.020
It's been a while since I last killed an investigator!

00:14:59.040 --> 00:15:00.440
Bitch!

00:15:21.030 --> 00:15:23.020
You're not getting away!

00:15:27.940 --> 00:15:29.400
Are they recording a TV show?

00:15:29.400 --> 00:15:31.240
No way.

00:15:31.240 --> 00:15:33.780
Hayamiya! Let's take that way out.

00:15:33.780 --> 00:15:35.210
Huh? Why?!

00:15:41.820 --> 00:15:46.290
That bastard Geega is only good at running away...

00:15:46.290 --> 00:15:47.560
Birdy.

00:15:47.560 --> 00:15:49.420
The period right before you
capture him is the most dangerous.

00:15:49.420 --> 00:15:50.630
I know that!

00:15:50.630 --> 00:15:52.620
Heat source dead ahead.

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:56.000
Tuto!

00:15:59.300 --> 00:16:01.240
That was close.

00:16:01.240 --> 00:16:03.070
So I missed?

00:16:18.290 --> 00:16:19.480
You bitch!

00:16:22.260 --> 00:16:27.850
This is... I found something
outrageous following Giga's trail.

00:16:31.200 --> 00:16:32.190
Oh, no...

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:40.880
That's an Entangle Blade.
It'll pass right through your biodefense shield.

00:16:40.880 --> 00:16:43.870
I'll rip you to pieces with this thing!

00:16:48.150 --> 00:16:50.550
Hmm... What now?

00:16:50.550 --> 00:16:52.620
Die!

00:16:52.620 --> 00:16:53.960
Got you!

00:16:53.960 --> 00:16:54.520
What?!

00:16:54.520 --> 00:16:57.860
Now come along quietly!

00:16:57.860 --> 00:16:59.700
Hurry!

00:16:59.700 --> 00:17:01.300
Look out!

00:17:01.300 --> 00:17:03.300
You're never escaping again!

00:17:03.300 --> 00:17:04.470
Huh?

00:17:04.470 --> 00:17:05.460
Shit!

00:17:07.640 --> 00:17:08.630
Shit!

00:17:14.710 --> 00:17:16.310
It's got to be a TV shoot after all!

00:17:16.310 --> 00:17:17.680
Stand back!

00:17:17.680 --> 00:17:20.550
Those brats, eh?

00:17:20.550 --> 00:17:22.540
I can use them!

00:17:23.690 --> 00:17:25.680
What? Senkawa!

00:17:27.920 --> 00:17:29.420
Hayamiya!

00:17:29.420 --> 00:17:31.420
She's coming, ain't she?

00:17:32.860 --> 00:17:34.100
Geega!

00:17:34.100 --> 00:17:36.090
Here I come, Altan!

00:17:46.240 --> 00:17:48.070
Birdy, no!

00:17:52.350 --> 00:17:55.350
<i>Who is this?</i>

00:17:55.350 --> 00:17:59.520
<i>Who is it, again? I feel like I've seen...</i>

00:17:59.520 --> 00:18:02.420
<i>Huh? Is this my hand...?</i>

00:18:02.420 --> 00:18:07.860
Hey, hang in there! Tuto!
Do something, Tuto! Tuto!

00:18:09.770 --> 00:18:12.870
<i>I feel kind of cold...</i>

00:18:12.870 --> 00:18:17.460
<i>This is weird. Could I be...?</i>

00:18:30.820 --> 00:18:34.810
What was that all about?
Talk about a crazy dream...

00:18:38.930 --> 00:18:40.330
Huh?

00:18:45.930 --> 00:18:47.340
Why?

00:18:47.340 --> 00:18:50.140
Tsutomu! How long are you going to sleep?!

00:18:50.140 --> 00:18:52.240
Mom and Dad are about to leave!

00:18:52.240 --> 00:18:53.640
Crap!

00:18:55.080 --> 00:18:57.580
Tsutomu, will you really be okay?

00:18:57.580 --> 00:19:01.080
I'm sorry, honey, but your
father is helpless by himself.

00:19:01.080 --> 00:19:02.580
